# This repository is checked out AS ~/.claude, a directory that also holds live
# runtime state and credentials. So the rule is allowlist, not denylist: ignore
# everything, then re-include only files this repo actually authors.
#
# A denylist would mean every new file Claude Code writes here shows up as
# untracked and one careless `git add -A` away from being published. That
# directory contains .credentials.json. Ignore-by-default is the safe direction.
#
# Verify after changing this file:
#   git check-ignore -v .credentials.json      # must print a match
#   git status --porcelain                     # must show only authored config

*

# --- Authored config: the contents of this repo ---
!.gitignore
!.github/
!.github/**
!agents/
!agents/**
!commands/
!commands/**
!hooks/
!hooks/**
!test/
!test/**

!CLAUDE.md
!guides/
!guides/**
!README.md
!LICENSE
!settings.example.json

# --- Machine-local tooling: re-ignored after the allowlist ---
# vexp hardcodes this machine's extension path and regenerates on every update.
hooks/vexp-*.sh
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.codex/
.vexp/

# --- Never, under any circumstances ---
# Re-ignored after the allowlist so no future rule above can expose them.
.credentials.json
.credentials.json.*
settings.json
settings.local.json
**/.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
